{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["And the reason for <b>\"I am not able, I alone\"</b> is not that the elders would help him to give them meat, for they have nothing. Furthermore, even when they have many officers, they complain only against Moses our teacher, who brought them out of Egypt, as is their custom, saying to him, \"Why have you brought us up from Egypt?\" — and it is he who must grant them all their requests through his prayer and bring their craving to them. But Moses thought that when they have many leaders, it will calm their anger and they will speak to their hearts at the time of their complaint. And it is possible that when the elders prophesied — those upon whom the spirit was placed when it was set upon them — and the people knew that they are proven as prophets, they would not all gather against Moses and would also ask their craving of them."], :book :numbers, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:04:20.168200316Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}